-- title:
--   Ribet's lemma: Hecke subring of index prime to p
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and assume that the weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ have an integral structure in the sense of [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6): the complex span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3), itself the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of those cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients $\mathrm{qCoeff}\,f\,n$ are rational integers, is the whole space $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$. Let $p$ be a prime, and let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers such that no prime belonging to $S$ divides $N$, and such that $p \neq 2$ in case $p \in S$. For a set $S$ of naturals, [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) denotes the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to the primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$; thus `heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅` is the full weight-two Hecke ring at level $N$. The assertion is that for every $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism $t$ of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ lying in `heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅` there exists a natural number $m$ with $p \nmid m$ and $m \cdot t \in$ `heckeAlgebra N 2 S`.
--
--   This is Ribet's lemma on the Hecke operators omitted at a finite set of primes: the subring generated by the Hecke operators away from $S$ has finite index prime to $p$ in the full weight-two Hecke ring, equivalently the two rings agree after tensoring with $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$. It is used to recover the operators $T_\ell$ at the finitely many auxiliary primes $\ell \in \Sigma$, and $T_p$ itself, in the Hecke-module arguments cited by [`CohCarrier.exists_ideal_forall_heckeAlg_baseChange_eq_smul_of_exists_jZero_pTorsion_eigenvector`](thm.html#CohCarrier.exists_ideal_forall_heckeAlg_baseChange_eq_smul_of_exists_jZero_pTorsion_eigenvector) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_apply_eq_pi_T_of_not_dvd_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_apply_eq_pi_T_of_not_dvd_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq).
